<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proofs of Properties <a href="#Thmproperty1" title="Property 1 (Loss–score Lipschitz link for GANs). ‣ 3.1 Linking Uniform Stability to Attack Scores ‣ 3 Stability–Based Analysis of MIA Risk in DP GANs and DP Diffusion Models ‣ On the MIA Vulnerability Gap Between Private GANs and Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and <a href="#Thmproperty2" title="Property 2 (Loss–score Lipschitz link for diffusion models). ‣ 3.1 Linking Uniform Stability to Attack Scores ‣ 3 Stability–Based Analysis of MIA Risk in DP GANs and DP Diffusion Models ‣ On the MIA Vulnerability Gap Between Private GANs and Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></h2>

<div id="Thmproperty1a" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_property">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproperty1a.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Property 1</span></span><span id="Thmproperty1a.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Loss–score Lipschitz link for GANs)<span id="Thmproperty1a.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproperty1a.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproperty1a.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproperty1a.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmproperty1a.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f=D_{\psi}\in\mathcal{F}_{\mathrm{GAN}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>GAN</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f=D_{\psi}\in\mathcal{F}_{\mathrm{GAN}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a discriminator parameterized by <math id="Thmproperty1a.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math>, trained using the logistic loss. For any input <math id="Thmproperty1a.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math> and label <math id="Thmproperty1a.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\{-1,+1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\{-1,+1\}</annotation></semantics></math>, define:</span></p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The </span><em id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph">score</em><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> used by the attacker is the raw logit: </span><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{f}(x):=D_{\psi}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{f}(x):=D_{\psi}(x)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The </span><em id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph">training loss</em><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is the logistic loss: </span><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(f,x,y):=\log(1+e^{-y\,s_{f}(x)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(f,x,y):=\log(1+e^{-y\,s_{f}(x)})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="Thmproperty1a.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproperty1a.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproperty1a.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume the loss values lie in a compact interval <math id="Thmproperty1a.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[a,b]\subset\mathbb{R}_{&gt;0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[a,b]\subset\mathbb{R}_{&gt;0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the map <math id="Thmproperty1a.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\mapsto s_{f}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\mapsto s_{f}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is Lipschitz with respect to <math id="Thmproperty1a.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(f,x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(f,x,y)</annotation></semantics></math>, with</span></p>
<table id="A1.E39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|s_{f}(x)-s_{f^{\prime}}(x)|\leq L_{s}\cdot|\ell(f,x,y)-\ell(f^{\prime},x,y)|," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|s_{f}(x)-s_{f^{\prime}}(x)|\leq L_{s}\cdot|\ell(f,x,y)-\ell(f^{\prime},x,y)|,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproperty1a.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproperty1a.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmproperty1a.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{s}=\sup_{u\in[a,b]}\frac{e^{u}}{e^{u}-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{s}=\sup_{u\in[a,b]}\frac{e^{u}}{e^{u}-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f=D_{\psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f=D_{\psi}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}=D_{\psi^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}=D_{\psi^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> be two discriminators in <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathrm{GAN}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>GAN</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathrm{GAN}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and fix any input <math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math>. Define the score function as the discriminator’s logit output:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{f}(x):=D_{\psi}(x),\qquad s_{f^{\prime}}(x):=D_{\psi^{\prime}}(x)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{f}(x):=D_{\psi}(x),\qquad s_{f^{\prime}}(x):=D_{\psi^{\prime}}(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Define the training loss on real data as:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(f,x,y):=\log(1+e^{-y\,s_{f}(x)},\ell(f^{\prime},x,y):=\log(1+e^{-ys_{f^{\prime}}(x)})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(f,x,y):=\log(1+e^{-y\,s_{f}(x)},\ell(f^{\prime},x,y):=\log(1+e^{-ys_{f^{\prime}}(x)}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(t):=\log(1+e^{-t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(t):=\log(1+e^{-t})</annotation></semantics></math>, so that <math id="A1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(f,x)=g(s_{f}(x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(f,x)=g(s_{f}(x))</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly decreasing and smooth, it is invertible on <math id="A1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℝ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>. Its inverse is given by:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{-1}(u)=-\log(e^{u}-1)\quad\text{for }u&gt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{-1}(u)=-\log(e^{u}-1)\quad\text{for }u&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="A1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> continuous and differentiable on <math id="A1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle y\cdot s_{f}(x)=g^{-1}(\ell(f,x,y))\Rightarrow s_{f}(x)=y\cdot g^{-1}(\ell(f,x,y))," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle y\cdot s_{f}(x)=g^{-1}(\ell(f,x,y))\Rightarrow s_{f}(x)=y\cdot g^{-1}(\ell(f,x,y)),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle s_{f^{\prime}}(x)=y\cdot g^{-1}(\ell(f^{\prime},x))." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle s_{f^{\prime}}(x)=y\cdot g^{-1}(\ell(f^{\prime},x)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">By the mean value theorem applied to <math id="A1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists <math id="A1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi\in[\ell(f,x,y),\ell(f^{\prime},x,y)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi\in[\ell(f,x,y),\ell(f^{\prime},x,y)]</annotation></semantics></math> such that:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|s_{f}(x)-s_{f^{\prime}}(x)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|s_{f}(x)-s_{f^{\prime}}(x)|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E45.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=|g^{-1}(\ell(f,x))-g^{-1}(\ell(f^{\prime},x))|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=|g^{-1}(\ell(f,x))-g^{-1}(\ell(f^{\prime},x))|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=|(g^{-1})^{\prime}(\xi)|\cdot|\ell(f,x,y)-\ell(f^{\prime},x,y)|." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=|(g^{-1})^{\prime}(\xi)|\cdot|\ell(f,x,y)-\ell(f^{\prime},x,y)|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We compute the derivative of <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(g^{-1})^{\prime}(u)=-\frac{e^{u}}{e^{u}-1},\quad\text{so}\quad|(g^{-1})^{\prime}(u)|=\frac{e^{u}}{e^{u}-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>so</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(g^{-1})^{\prime}(u)=-\frac{e^{u}}{e^{u}-1},\quad\text{so}\quad|(g^{-1})^{\prime}(u)|=\frac{e^{u}}{e^{u}-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Assume that the loss values <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(f,x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(f,x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(f^{\prime},x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(f^{\prime},x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> lie in a compact interval <math id="A1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[a,b]\subset(0,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[a,b]\subset(0,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the quantity <math id="A1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{e^{u}}{e^{u}-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{e^{u}}{e^{u}-1}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded on <math id="A1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[a,b]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[a,b]</annotation></semantics></math>, since it is continuous on the compact interval <math id="A1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[a,b]\subset(0,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[a,b]\subset(0,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math>, and we define:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{s}:=\sup_{u\in[a,b]}\frac{e^{u}}{e^{u}-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{s}:=\sup_{u\in[a,b]}\frac{e^{u}}{e^{u}-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(48)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">It follows that:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|s_{f}(x)-s_{f^{\prime}}(x)|\leq L_{s}\cdot|\ell(f,x,y)-\ell(f^{\prime},x,y)|," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|s_{f}(x)-s_{f^{\prime}}(x)|\leq L_{s}\cdot|\ell(f,x,y)-\ell(f^{\prime},x,y)|,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(49)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmproperty2a" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_property">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproperty2a.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Property 2</span></span><span id="Thmproperty2a.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Loss–score Lipschitz link for diffusion models)<span id="Thmproperty2a.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproperty2a.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproperty2a.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproperty2a.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmproperty2a.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f=\epsilon_{\theta}\in\mathcal{F}_{\mathrm{Diff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>Diff</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f=\epsilon_{\theta}\in\mathcal{F}_{\mathrm{Diff}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a denoising network parameterized by <math id="Thmproperty2a.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>, trained using the EDM objective (Equation <a href="#A1.E51" title="In 2nd item ‣ Property 2 (Loss–score Lipschitz link for diffusion models). ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Properties and ‣ On the MIA Vulnerability Gap Between Private GANs and Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">51</span></a>) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Karras et al. 2022</a>)</cite>. Define:</span></p>
<ul id="A1.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">the </span><em id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph">attack score</em><span id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> as the scalar denoising error:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{f}(x):=\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon,\sigma}\left\|\epsilon_{\theta}(x+\sigma\epsilon,\sigma)-\epsilon\right\|^{2};" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{f}(x):=\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon,\sigma}\left\|\epsilon_{\theta}(x+\sigma\epsilon,\sigma)-\epsilon\right\|^{2};</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(50)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">the </span><em id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph">training loss</em><span id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> as the noise-weighted EDM objective:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(f,x):=\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon,\sigma}\left[\lambda(\sigma)\cdot\left\|\epsilon_{\theta}(x+\sigma\epsilon,\sigma)-\epsilon\right\|^{2}\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(f,x):=\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon,\sigma}\left[\lambda(\sigma)\cdot\left\|\epsilon_{\theta}(x+\sigma\epsilon,\sigma)-\epsilon\right\|^{2}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(51)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I2.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where </span><math id="A1.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda(\sigma)\in[\lambda_{\min},\lambda_{\max}]\subset(0,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda(\sigma)\in[\lambda_{\min},\lambda_{\max}]\subset(0,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i2.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is a bounded weighting function.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="Thmproperty2a.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproperty2a.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, for any <math id="Thmproperty2a.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f,f^{\prime}\in\mathcal{F}_{\mathrm{Diff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>Diff</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f,f^{\prime}\in\mathcal{F}_{\mathrm{Diff}}</annotation></semantics></math> and any <math id="Thmproperty2a.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math>, the following inequality holds:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|s_{f}(x)-s_{f^{\prime}}(x)|\leq\frac{1}{\lambda_{\min}}\cdot\left\|\ell(f,\cdot)-\ell(f^{\prime},\cdot)\right\|_{\infty}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|s_{f}(x)-s_{f^{\prime}}(x)|\leq\frac{1}{\lambda_{\min}}\cdot\left\|\ell(f,\cdot)-\ell(f^{\prime},\cdot)\right\|_{\infty}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(52)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproperty2a.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproperty2a.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">That is, the attack score is <math id="Thmproperty2a.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\min}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\min}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz with respect to the training loss.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f=\epsilon_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f=\epsilon_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}=\epsilon_{\theta^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}=\epsilon_{\theta^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> be two denoising networks in <math id="A1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathrm{Diff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>Diff</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathrm{Diff}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and fix an input <math id="A1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">We define the attack score as:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{f}(x):=\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon,\sigma}\left\|\epsilon_{\theta}(x+\sigma\epsilon,\sigma)-\epsilon\right\|^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{f}(x):=\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon,\sigma}\left\|\epsilon_{\theta}(x+\sigma\epsilon,\sigma)-\epsilon\right\|^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(53)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">and the training loss as:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(f,x):=\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon,\sigma}\left[\lambda(\sigma)\cdot\left\|\epsilon_{\theta}(x+\sigma\epsilon,\sigma)-\epsilon\right\|^{2}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(f,x):=\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon,\sigma}\left[\lambda(\sigma)\cdot\left\|\epsilon_{\theta}(x+\sigma\epsilon,\sigma)-\epsilon\right\|^{2}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(54)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let us denote:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{f}(x,\epsilon,\sigma):=\left\|\epsilon_{\theta}(x+\sigma\epsilon,\sigma)-\epsilon\right\|^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{f}(x,\epsilon,\sigma):=\left\|\epsilon_{\theta}(x+\sigma\epsilon,\sigma)-\epsilon\right\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(55)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then we can write:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{f}(x)=\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon,\sigma}[a_{f}(x,\epsilon,\sigma)],\quad\ell(f,x)=\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon,\sigma}[\lambda(\sigma)\cdot a_{f}(x,\epsilon,\sigma)]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{f}(x)=\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon,\sigma}[a_{f}(x,\epsilon,\sigma)],\quad\ell(f,x)=\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon,\sigma}[\lambda(\sigma)\cdot a_{f}(x,\epsilon,\sigma)].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(56)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda(\sigma)\in[\lambda_{\min},\lambda_{\max}]\subset(0,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda(\sigma)\in[\lambda_{\min},\lambda_{\max}]\subset(0,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math>, for all <math id="A1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,\epsilon,\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,\epsilon,\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\min}\cdot a_{f}(x,\epsilon,\sigma)\leq\lambda(\sigma)\cdot a_{f}(x,\epsilon,\sigma)\leq\lambda_{\max}\cdot a_{f}(x,\epsilon,\sigma)\quad." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1.000em;" width="1.000em"></mspace><mo>.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\min}\cdot a_{f}(x,\epsilon,\sigma)\leq\lambda(\sigma)\cdot a_{f}(x,\epsilon,\sigma)\leq\lambda_{\max}\cdot a_{f}(x,\epsilon,\sigma)\quad.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(57)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Taking expectation over <math id="A1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\epsilon,\sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\epsilon,\sigma)</annotation></semantics></math>, we get:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\min}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon,\sigma}[a_{f}(x,\epsilon,\sigma)]\leq\ell(f,x)\leq\lambda_{\max}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon,\sigma}[a_{f}(x,\epsilon,\sigma)]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\min}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon,\sigma}[a_{f}(x,\epsilon,\sigma)]\leq\ell(f,x)\leq\lambda_{\max}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon,\sigma}[a_{f}(x,\epsilon,\sigma)].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(58)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">By definition of <math id="A1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{f}(x)=\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon,\sigma}[a_{f}(x,\epsilon,\sigma)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{f}(x)=\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon,\sigma}[a_{f}(x,\epsilon,\sigma)]</annotation></semantics></math>, this gives:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\min}\cdot s_{f}(x)\leq\ell(f,x)\leq\lambda_{\max}\cdot s_{f}(x)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\min}\cdot s_{f}(x)\leq\ell(f,x)\leq\lambda_{\max}\cdot s_{f}(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(59)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, dividing through and using the positivity of <math id="A1.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>, we conclude, pointwise in <math id="A1.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\max}^{-1}\cdot\ell(f,x)\leq s_{f}(x)\leq\lambda_{\min}^{-1}\cdot\ell(f,x)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>max</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\max}^{-1}\cdot\ell(f,x)\leq s_{f}(x)\leq\lambda_{\min}^{-1}\cdot\ell(f,x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(60)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Similarly, for the difference between two models:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|s_{f}(x)-s_{f^{\prime}}(x)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|s_{f}(x)-s_{f^{\prime}}(x)|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E61.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left|\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon,\sigma}\left[a_{f}(x,\epsilon,\sigma)-a_{f^{\prime}}(x,\epsilon,\sigma)\right]\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left|\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon,\sigma}\left[a_{f}(x,\epsilon,\sigma)-a_{f^{\prime}}(x,\epsilon,\sigma)\right]\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(61)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon,\sigma}\left|a_{f}(x,\epsilon,\sigma)-a_{f^{\prime}}(x,\epsilon,\sigma)\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon,\sigma}\left|a_{f}(x,\epsilon,\sigma)-a_{f^{\prime}}(x,\epsilon,\sigma)\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(62)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\lambda_{\min}^{-1}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon,\sigma}\left|\lambda(\sigma)\cdot a_{f}(x,\epsilon,\sigma)-\lambda(\sigma)\cdot a_{f^{\prime}}(x,\epsilon,\sigma)\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\lambda_{\min}^{-1}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon,\sigma}\left|\lambda(\sigma)\cdot a_{f}(x,\epsilon,\sigma)-\lambda(\sigma)\cdot a_{f^{\prime}}(x,\epsilon,\sigma)\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(63)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\lambda_{\min}^{-1}\cdot\left|\ell(f,x)-\ell(f^{\prime},x)\right|." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\lambda_{\min}^{-1}\cdot\left|\ell(f,x)-\ell(f^{\prime},x)\right|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(64)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">Taking the supremum over <math id="A1.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E65" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|s_{f}(x)-s_{f^{\prime}}(x)|\leq\lambda_{\min}^{-1}\cdot\|\ell(f,\cdot)-\ell(f^{\prime},\cdot)\|_{\infty}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|s_{f}(x)-s_{f^{\prime}}(x)|\leq\lambda_{\min}^{-1}\cdot\|\ell(f,\cdot)-\ell(f^{\prime},\cdot)\|_{\infty}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(65)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, the property holds with Lipschitz constant <math id="A1.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{s}:=\lambda_{\min}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{s}:=\lambda_{\min}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, completing the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Proof of Theorem 1</h2>

<div id="A2.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=\{x_{1},\dots,x_{m}\}\sim\mathcal{P}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=\{x_{1},\dots,x_{m}\}\sim\mathcal{P}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> be the training dataset, and let <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\sim\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\sim\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math> be an independent sample. Fix <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,\dots,m\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,\dots,m\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{\setminus i}=D\setminus\{x_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{\setminus i}=D\setminus\{x_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math> be the neighboring dataset obtained by removing <math id="A2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">By definition, the membership advantage of the adversary <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> is</span></p>
<table id="A2.E66" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{ADV}_{\texttt{MIA}}=\left|\Pr[\mathcal{A}(x_{i})=1\mid x_{i}\in D]-\Pr[\mathcal{A}(x)=1\mid x\notin D]\right|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ADV</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">MIA</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{ADV}_{\texttt{MIA}}=\left|\Pr[\mathcal{A}(x_{i})=1\mid x_{i}\in D]-\Pr[\mathcal{A}(x)=1\mid x\notin D]\right|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(66)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">We analyze this by comparing the adversary’s predictions on models trained on <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> and on <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{\setminus i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{\setminus i}</annotation></semantics></math>. By Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Score stability). ‣ 3.1 Linking Uniform Stability to Attack Scores ‣ 3 Stability–Based Analysis of MIA Risk in DP GANs and DP Diffusion Models ‣ On the MIA Vulnerability Gap Between Private GANs and Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, the score function satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A2.E67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|s_{f_{D}}(x)-s_{f_{D^{\setminus i}}}(x)|\leq L_{s}\beta\quad\text{for all }x\in\mathcal{X}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|s_{f_{D}}(x)-s_{f_{D^{\setminus i}}}(x)|\leq L_{s}\beta\quad\text{for all }x\in\mathcal{X}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(67)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">This implies that the adversary’s predictions can differ only when the score is within <math id="A2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{s}\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{s}\beta</annotation></semantics></math> of the threshold <math id="A2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>, that is:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E68.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{I}\{s_{f_{D}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{I}\{s_{f_{D}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E68.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\tau\}\neq\mathbb{I}\{s_{f_{D^{\setminus i}}}(x)\leq\tau\}\quad" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\tau\}\neq\mathbb{I}\{s_{f_{D^{\setminus i}}}(x)\leq\tau\}\quad</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(68)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Rightarrow\quad s_{f_{D}}(x)\in(\tau-L_{s}\beta,\tau+L_{s}\beta)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Rightarrow\quad s_{f_{D}}(x)\in(\tau-L_{s}\beta,\tau+L_{s}\beta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(69)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Define the margin region <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=(\tau-L_{s}\beta,\tau+L_{s}\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=(\tau-L_{s}\beta,\tau+L_{s}\beta)</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose <math id="A2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{f_{D}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{f_{D}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> admits a probability density function <math id="A2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> bounded above by <math id="A2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="A2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(u)\leq Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(u)\leq Q</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the difference in prediction probabilities satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A2.E70" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E70.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\left|\Pr[\mathcal{A}(x_{i})=1]-\Pr[\mathcal{A}(x)=1]\right|\leq\Pr[s_{f_{D}}(x)\in M]\leq 2QL_{s}\beta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\Pr[\mathcal{A}(x_{i})=1]-\Pr[\mathcal{A}(x)=1]\right|\leq\Pr[s_{f_{D}}(x)\in M]\leq 2QL_{s}\beta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(70)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Indeed, since <math id="A2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(u)\leq Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(u)\leq Q</annotation></semantics></math>, the probability mass in the margin region <math id="A2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> is at most:</span></p>
<table id="A2.E71" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E71.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr[s_{f_{D}}(x)\in M]\leq\int_{\tau-L_{s}\beta}^{\tau+L_{s}\beta}p(u)\,du\leq 2QL_{s}\beta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr[s_{f_{D}}(x)\in M]\leq\int_{\tau-L_{s}\beta}^{\tau+L_{s}\beta}p(u)\,du\leq 2QL_{s}\beta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(71)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">More details on Equation <a href="#A2.E70" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem 1 ‣ On the MIA Vulnerability Gap Between Private GANs and Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">70</span></a> are provided below
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Comments Eq. <a href="#A2.E70" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem 1 ‣ On the MIA Vulnerability Gap Between Private GANs and Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">70</span></a>.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let’s give more details on how we obtained the following:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\left|\Pr[\mathcal{A}(z_{i})=1]-\Pr[\mathcal{A}(z)=1]\right|\leq\Pr[s_{f_{D}}(x)\in M]\leq 2QL_{s}\beta," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\Pr[\mathcal{A}(z_{i})=1]-\Pr[\mathcal{A}(z)=1]\right|\leq\Pr[s_{f_{D}}(x)\in M]\leq 2QL_{s}\beta,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{A}(x)=\mathbb{I}\{s_{f_{D}}(x)\leq\tau\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}(x)=\mathbb{I}\{s_{f_{D}}(x)\leq\tau\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=[\tau-L_{s}\beta,\tau+L_{s}\beta]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=[\tau-L_{s}\beta,\tau+L_{s}\beta]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">First inequality.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(x):=s_{f_{D}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(x):=s_{f_{D}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{\prime}(x):=s_{f_{D^{\setminus i}}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{\prime}(x):=s_{f_{D^{\setminus i}}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the only difference in the adversary’s behavior arises from training on or excluding <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, the output of <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> can only change if the score lies near the threshold. We formalize this as:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E72"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E72.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\left|\Pr[\mathcal{A}(z_{i})=1]-\Pr[\mathcal{A}(z)=1]\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|\Pr[\mathcal{A}(z_{i})=1]-\Pr[\mathcal{A}(z)=1]\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(72)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E73"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E73.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\left|\mathbb{E}_{x_{i}}[\mathbb{I}\{s(x_{i})\leq\tau\}]-\mathbb{E}_{x}[\mathbb{I}\{s^{\prime}(x)\leq\tau\}]\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left|\mathbb{E}_{x_{i}}[\mathbb{I}\{s(x_{i})\leq\tau\}]-\mathbb{E}_{x}[\mathbb{I}\{s^{\prime}(x)\leq\tau\}]\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(73)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E74"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E74.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{P}}\left|\mathbb{I}\{s(x)\leq\tau\}-\mathbb{I}\{s^{\prime}(x)\leq\tau\}\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{P}}\left|\mathbb{I}\{s(x)\leq\tau\}-\mathbb{I}\{s^{\prime}(x)\leq\tau\}\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(74)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E75"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E75.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{P}}\left[\mathbb{I}\{|s(x)-\tau|\leq|s(x)-s^{\prime}(x)|\}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{P}}\left[\mathbb{I}\{|s(x)-\tau|\leq|s(x)-s^{\prime}(x)|\}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(75)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E76"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E76.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\Pr\left[|s(x)-\tau|\leq L_{s}\cdot\|\ell(f_{D},\cdot)-\ell(f_{D^{\setminus i}},\cdot)\|_{\infty}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\Pr\left[|s(x)-\tau|\leq L_{s}\cdot\|\ell(f_{D},\cdot)-\ell(f_{D^{\setminus i}},\cdot)\|_{\infty}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(76)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E77"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E77.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\Pr\left[s_{f_{D}}(x)\in[\tau-L_{s}\beta,\tau+L_{s}\beta]\right]=\Pr[s_{f_{D}}(x)\in M]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\Pr\left[s_{f_{D}}(x)\in[\tau-L_{s}\beta,\tau+L_{s}\beta]\right]=\Pr[s_{f_{D}}(x)\in M],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(77)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where we used the Lipschitz assumption on the score and the uniform stability bound <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\ell(f_{D},\cdot)-\ell(f_{D^{\setminus i}},\cdot)\|_{\infty}\leq\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\ell(f_{D},\cdot)-\ell(f_{D^{\setminus i}},\cdot)\|_{\infty}\leq\beta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Second inequality.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The bound <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr[s_{f_{D}}(x)\in M]\leq 2QL_{s}\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr[s_{f_{D}}(x)\in M]\leq 2QL_{s}\beta</annotation></semantics></math> requires a regularity condition on the distribution of the score <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{f_{D}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{f_{D}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>. We assume <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{f_{D}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{f_{D}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> admits a probability density function <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> bounded above by some constant <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>, then</p>
<table id="A2.E78" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E78.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr[s_{f_{D}}(x)\in M]\leq Q\cdot|M|=2QL_{s}\beta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>M</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr[s_{f_{D}}(x)\in M]\leq Q\cdot|M|=2QL_{s}\beta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(78)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Alternatively, the inequality may be interpreted in a worst-case sense, assuming that the measure of any margin region of width <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2L_{s}\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2L_{s}\beta</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded proportionally.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In our settings, the assumption is satisfied in practice. For diffusion models trained via the EDM objective, the score <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{f_{D}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{f_{D}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is the expected denoising error, which is a smooth, noise-averaged functional of the input and thus likely admits a bounded density on <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>. For GANs, the score is typically the (logit) output of the discriminator, which is a continuous function of <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and similarly expected to induce a smooth distribution. In both cases, the bounded-density assumption required for the margin bound holds in practice.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Additional Discussion on Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Bound on membership advantage under uniform score stability). ‣ 3.2 Stability Bound on Membership Advantage ‣ 3 Stability–Based Analysis of MIA Risk in DP GANs and DP Diffusion Models ‣ On the MIA Vulnerability Gap Between Private GANs and Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The bound established in Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Bound on membership advantage under uniform score stability). ‣ 3.2 Stability Bound on Membership Advantage ‣ 3 Stability–Based Analysis of MIA Risk in DP GANs and DP Diffusion Models ‣ On the MIA Vulnerability Gap Between Private GANs and Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> states that, under uniform stability and Lipschitz continuity of the score with respect to the loss, the membership advantage of any threshold-based adversary is bounded as</p>
<table id="A3.E79" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{ADV}_{\texttt{MIA}}\leq 2QL_{s}\beta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ADV</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">MIA</mtext></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{ADV}_{\texttt{MIA}}\leq 2QL_{s}\beta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(79)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">To ensure that this bound is non-trivial (i.e., strictly less than 1), it is necessary that <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2QL_{s}\beta&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2QL_{s}\beta&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>. This condition introduces a trade-off between the score sensitivity <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>, the stability <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, and the score density upper bound <math id="A3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>, which we now analyze in more detail.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Stability <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The uniform stability parameter <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> quantifies how much the loss <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(f_{D},z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(f_{D},z)</annotation></semantics></math> changes when one training point is removed from the dataset. For DP-SGD with per-sample gradient clipping at norm <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>, the expected uniform stability can be upper bounded as</p>
<table id="A3.E80" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{1}{m}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\alpha_{t}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{1}{m}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\alpha_{t}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(80)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> is the dataset size, <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of training steps, and <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> are the learning rates. Hence, increasing <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> or decaying the learning rate can help reduce <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, thereby tightening the membership advantage bound.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Lipschitz constant <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The constant <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> reflects the sensitivity of the attack score to changes in the loss. Its value depends on the model architecture and the type of score used by the attacker:</p>
<ul id="A3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In diffusion models, the score is the per-sample denoising error <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{f}(x)=\|\epsilon_{\theta}(x+\sigma\epsilon,\sigma)-\epsilon\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{f}(x)=\|\epsilon_{\theta}(x+\sigma\epsilon,\sigma)-\epsilon\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, directly derived from the loss. However, due to the multiplicative noise and squared error scaling, <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> can be large, especially when the noise level <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> is small.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In GANs, the attack score is the raw discriminator logit <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, and the loss is binary cross-entropy with logits. Thus, <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to the inverse derivative of the sigmoid and may remain moderate depending on the activation range of the discriminator.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Large <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> weakens the bound and may dominate the overall expression when the score is highly sensitive to training perturbations.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Density bound <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The constant <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> assumes that the score <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{f}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{f}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> admits a probability density function bounded above by <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>. This assumption holds for most smooth neural networks with continuous outputs, and <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> reflects the worst-case concentration of the score distribution. In practice, <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> is often moderate unless the score is extremely peaked.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Implication.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The bound <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{ADV}_{\texttt{MIA}}\leq 2QL_{s}\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ADV</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">MIA</mtext></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{ADV}_{\texttt{MIA}}\leq 2QL_{s}\beta</annotation></semantics></math> is informative when all three factors are controlled. In particular, for a fixed model class, reducing <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> via larger datasets or improved stability (e.g., via regularization or differential privacy) is essential to keep the membership advantage small. At the same time, careful design of the score function (e.g., smooth denoising metrics, logit clipping) may help reduce <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>. This trade-off reflects the fundamental connection between algorithmic stability and the susceptibility of a model to inference attacks.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Additional Comments on Common Randomness (Lemma 2)</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Coupled noise.</span> Uniform stability compares two runs of DP–SGD on neighbouring datasets
<math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{\setminus i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{\setminus i}</annotation></semantics></math> that differ in one example.
To isolate the <em id="A4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">data</em> effect, we <em id="A4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">couple</em> the randomness:
the two executions use the <span id="A4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">same</span> mini–batches
<math id="A4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and the <span id="A4.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">same</span> Gaussian noise vectors
<math id="A4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{t}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2}I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{t}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2}I)</annotation></semantics></math> for every step <math id="A4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.
With this coupling, the parameter updates are</p>
<table id="A4.E81" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{t+1}=\theta_{t}-\alpha_{t}\!\bigl(g_{t}+\eta_{t}\bigr),\qquad\theta^{\prime}_{t+1}=\theta^{\prime}_{t}-\alpha_{t}\!\bigl(g^{\prime}_{t}+\eta_{t}\bigr)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t+1}=\theta_{t}-\alpha_{t}\!\bigl(g_{t}+\eta_{t}\bigr),\qquad\theta^{\prime}_{t+1}=\theta^{\prime}_{t}-\alpha_{t}\!\bigl(g^{\prime}_{t}+\eta_{t}\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(81)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where
<math id="A4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{t}:=\tfrac{1}{b}\sum_{j\in B_{t}}\!\operatorname{clip}\bigl(\nabla\ell(f_{\theta_{t}},z_{j}),C\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>b</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>clip</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{t}:=\tfrac{1}{b}\sum_{j\in B_{t}}\!\operatorname{clip}\bigl(\nabla\ell(f_{\theta_{t}},z_{j}),C\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math>
and likewise for <math id="A4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\prime}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\prime}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{t}:=\theta_{t}-\theta^{\prime}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{t}:=\theta_{t}-\theta^{\prime}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Because the noise terms cancel,</p>
<table id="A4.E82" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{t+1}=\Delta_{t}-\alpha_{t}\,(g_{t}-g^{\prime}_{t})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{t+1}=\Delta_{t}-\alpha_{t}\,(g_{t}-g^{\prime}_{t}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(82)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">and thus <math id="A4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta_{t+1}\|\leq\|\Delta_{t}\|+\alpha_{t}\,C/m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta_{t+1}\|\leq\|\Delta_{t}\|+\alpha_{t}\,C/m</annotation></semantics></math>,
since the differing example appears in the batch with probability <math id="A4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b/m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b/m</annotation></semantics></math>.
Iterating over <math id="A4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> steps yields</p>
<table id="A4.E83" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta_{T}\|\;\leq\;\frac{C}{m}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\alpha_{t}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>C</mi><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta_{T}\|\;\leq\;\frac{C}{m}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\alpha_{t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(83)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p1.4" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(\cdot;z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(\cdot;z)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A4.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz in <math id="A4.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A4.E84" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\ell(f_{D},z)-\ell(f_{D^{\setminus i}},z)|\;\leq\;L\,\|\Delta_{T}\|\;\leq\;\frac{LC}{m}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\alpha_{t}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\ell(f_{D},z)-\ell(f_{D^{\setminus i}},z)|\;\leq\;L\,\|\Delta_{T}\|\;\leq\;\frac{LC}{m}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\alpha_{t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(84)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p1.5" class="ltx_p">which gives the classical bound
<math id="A4.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\beta\leq\frac{2LC}{m}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\alpha_{t}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\beta\leq\frac{2LC}{m}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\alpha_{t}.</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Uncoupled noise.</span>
If the two runs draw <em id="A4.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">independent</em> noise
<math id="A4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta^{\prime}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta^{\prime}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>,
then
<math id="A4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{t+1}=\Delta_{t}-\alpha_{t}(g_{t}-g^{\prime}_{t})-\alpha_{t}(\eta_{t}-\eta^{\prime}_{t})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{t+1}=\Delta_{t}-\alpha_{t}(g_{t}-g^{\prime}_{t})-\alpha_{t}(\eta_{t}-\eta^{\prime}_{t}),</annotation></semantics></math>
so <math id="A4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta_{T}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta_{T}\|</annotation></semantics></math> acquires an additional
random-walk term of order <math id="A4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\sigma\sqrt{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>T</mi></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\sigma\sqrt{T}</annotation></semantics></math>.
A typical uncoupled bound therefore becomes</p>
<table id="A4.E85" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\leq\frac{2LC}{m}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\alpha_{t}+\mathcal{O}(\alpha\sigma\sqrt{T}\bigr)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>T</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\leq\frac{2LC}{m}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\alpha_{t}+\mathcal{O}(\alpha\sigma\sqrt{T}\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(85)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">explicitly reflecting the dependence on the DP noise scale <math id="A4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Implementation Details</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For GANs, we follow the training procedure and hyperparameter configuration from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bie, Kamath, and Zhang (2023)</a></cite>, including the same discriminator and generator architectures, optimizer settings, and training schedule. For diffusion models, we build upon the DP EDM-based setup introduced by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dockhorn et al. (2023)</a></cite>, with minor architectural simplifications to ensure stable training on a single GPU. Specifically, we reduce the base number of channels from 128 to 32, use fewer residual blocks per resolution (2 instead of 4), adopt a simplified channel multiplier schedule of <math id="A5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[1,1,1,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[1,1,1,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, and set the embedding channel multiplier to <math id="A5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math>. We also restrict attention to the lowest spatial resolution (<math id="A5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4\times 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\times 4</annotation></semantics></math> instead of <math id="A5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16\times 16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16\times 16</annotation></semantics></math>). We use a fixed dropout rate of 0.1 and a batch size of 128. The model is trained using DP-SGD for 300 epochs with a learning rate of 0.0003 across all privacy levels (<math id="A5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\in\{\infty,10,5,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\in\{\infty,10,5,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>). To improve training signal, we use a noise multiplicity of 32 loss terms per image, sampled at varying noise levels. We train 20 independent shadow models. At inference, we generate samples using 150 denoising steps with sampling parameters <math id="A5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\min}=0.002" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.002</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\min}=0.002</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\max}=80" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>80</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\max}=80</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=7.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=7.0</annotation></semantics></math>, and guidance scale <math id="A5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3.0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Attack Evaluation</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To assess the effectiveness of membership inference attacks, we report five standard classification metrics: accuracy, precision, true positive rate (TPR), false positive rate (FPR), and area under the ROC curve (AUC). Accuracy measures the overall proportion of correctly classified examples (both members and non-members). Precision reflects the proportion of true members among the samples predicted as members, capturing the attacker’s confidence in positive predictions. TPR (also known as recall or sensitivity) quantifies the fraction of true members correctly identified by the attack. FPR measures the fraction of non-members that are incorrectly predicted as members, and should ideally remain low. Finally, AUC evaluates the attack’s ability to distinguish members from non-members across all possible thresholds; it is a threshold-independent metric where a value of 0.5 corresponds to random guessing. Higher values of accuracy, precision, TPR, and AUC indicate stronger attack performance, whereas lower FPR values are preferable.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Notations</h2>

<figure id="A7.T3" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A7.T3.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A7.T3.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A7.T3.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="A7.T3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Symbol</span></th>
<th id="A7.T3.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A7.T3.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Type</span></th>
<th id="A7.T3.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A7.T3.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Description</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A7.T3.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A7.T3.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t"><math id="A7.T3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A7.T3.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Space</td>
<td id="A7.T3.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Input space (e.g., images)</td></tr>
<tr id="A7.T3.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A7.T3.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><math id="A7.T3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}\subset\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}\subset\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A7.T3.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Space</td>
<td id="A7.T3.1.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Output space (e.g., logits, scores)</td></tr>
<tr id="A7.T3.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A7.T3.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><math id="A7.T3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A7.T3.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Dist.</td>
<td id="A7.T3.1.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Data distribution</td></tr>
<tr id="A7.T3.1.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A7.T3.1.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><math id="A7.T3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=\{x_{i}\}_{i=1}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=\{x_{i}\}_{i=1}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A7.T3.1.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Dataset</td>
<td id="A7.T3.1.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Training set of size <math id="A7.T3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A7.T3.1.6" class="ltx_tr">
